 ],
 "literal": "The male deer, embracing the gentle female deer, with intense desire, / having hidden and huddled in the bushes of the forest, / the noble male elephant with a trunk, joining with his female elephant, / reaches the mountain side adorned with dark clouds, / evening has come, along with the great rain of the rainy season; / he who ruined the fine beauty of my gold-like complexion, / if he still does not return, / O friend, what will become of the state of our sweet life?",
 "translation": "The male deer, embracing his gentle mate with deep desire, hides and huddles in the forest bushes. The great elephant with a trunk joins his female mate and reaches the mountain slopes adorned with dark clouds. Evening has arrived, bringing the heavy rains of the season. If he, who ruined the fine beauty of my gold-like complexion, still does not return, O friend, what will become of our sweet life?",
 "modern": "ஆண் மான் தன் மென்மையான பெண் மானைத் தழுவிக்கொண்டு, மிகுந்த காதலோடு காட்டில் உள்ள புதருக்குள் மறைந்து ஒடுங்கவும், துதிக்கையையுடைய நல்ல ஆண் யானை தன் பெண் யானையோடு கூடி மேகங்கள் சூழ்ந்த மலைப்பக்கத்தை அடையவும், மழைக் காலத்துப் பெருமழையோடு மாலைப் பொழுது வந்துவிட்டது. பொன்னைப் போன்ற என் உடலின் அழகைச் சிதைத்தவர் இன்னும் வரவில்லை என்றால், தோழியே! நம்முடைய இனிய உயிரின் நிலை என்னவாகும்?",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend in deep distress. The rainy season has arrived, which is the promised time for the hero's return, but he is still absent. She observes the natural world around her, where animals are uniting in love: the male deer embraces its mate and huddles in the bushes, and the male elephant joins its female on the cloudy mountain slopes. These images of union belong to the Mullai landscape and intensify her sense of loneliness during the evening. She despairs that if her lover, who caused her beauty to fade through separation, does not return now, her very life may not survive.",
